uncertainties, as indicated by differences in the inferred
parameters between signal models. The primary black hole lies
within or above the theorized mass gap where black holes between
60─130 M$_{{\ensuremath{\odot}}}$ should be rare, due to pair-
instability mechanisms, while the secondary spans the gap. The
observation of GW231123 therefore suggests the formation of
black holes from channels beyond standard stellar collapse and
that intermediate-mass black holes of mass
{\ensuremath{\sim}}200 M$_{{\ensuremath{\odot}}}$ form through
gravitational-wave-driven mergers.}},
